ompensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Sweetgreen, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $1.5B market cap on $679M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -56% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $119M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -7332.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 3.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (23.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 28% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Cyclical peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 345% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Insiders are net buyers (86% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $3.1M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Responsive Playbooks and the SG Inflection","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/139/Responsive_Playbooks_and_the_SG_Inflection_111326011202_1794593522.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794593522.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.612,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Are Retail-Wholesale Stocks Lagging  Sweetgreen (SG) This Year?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3027311/are-retail-wholesale-stocks-lagging-sweetgreen-sg-this-year?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_1-3027311","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794318001.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Makes Sweetgreen, Inc. (SG) a Strong Momentum Stock: Buy Now?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3026634/what-makes-sweetgreen-inc-sg-a-strong-momentum